    "independentFindings": [
      "The completed Arcane Grappler research conclusion is readable on both book pages, with original parchment and recipe icons; no development/server-check/mockup/QA labels appear inside gameplay pixels.",
      "The three bench images show post-payment empty grids, visible physical tip/spool/gun icons and aura 4975/4950/4875 respectively. They are consistent after-craft views; the native log, rather than the empty-grid images alone, establishes exact original materials, crystals and payment.",
      "The pedestal view shows the textured three-dimensional gun on the native recharge pedestal without missing-texture checkerboards, broken meshes or an invented gun GUI. The log ties this to actual native charging of the same paid item, not a supplied charged tool.",
      "The main-hand flight image visibly contains the hook, additive colored glow and textured four-sided rope against the stone wall. Main-hand and off-hand pull views both show a connected rope on the corresponding side and the held gun orientation. No apparent asset corruption, dangling untextured geometry or developer overlay was found.",
      "The rope is noticeably dark in both anchored pull views while bright during flight. Current native tube lighting samples hook packed light for the whole tube. Released RenderGrapple assigns light220 to glow vertices but does not explicitly disable GLE lighting or assign a new global rope lightmap, so the primary source does not establish a fullbright-rope requirement. This observation is retained as a lighting adaptation limit, not silently removed from the review.",
      "The release and replacement captures retain the correct held gun appearances and show ordinary gameplay after real movement. Close stone wall views make the new projectile itself hard to assess in the replacement frame; the matching native old209/new211/one-active-hook observation establishes replacement behavior.",
      "The complete sheet includes all11 current native frames, and the six-frame preview covers study, pedestal, flight, both hands and replacement. Captions are outside the native gameplay pixels, legible and accurately describe their route context."
    ],
    "independentLimits": [
      "Supplied precursors BASEARTIFICE/RECHARGEPEDESTAL, raw theories/nugget/crafting materials/crystals, initial aura, arena, anchor wall, workbench and pedestal are explicit QA fixtures. These frames are not a full ordinary survival playthrough, independent multiplayer/client reload test or audible-sound proof.",
      "Exact theory/material/crystal/Vis/charge debits and movement magnitudes require the matching native callback log; a still image does not establish them independently. The log reports paidStudy1, three paid benches125Vis, native pedestal100charge, three native shots and final97charge on one paid gun.",
      "Native rope buffers adapt removed GLE tessellation and lighting. Whole-tube hook packed-light sampling can darken the entire rope when the anchor is inside stone; per-segment light, binary-identical GLE normals/caps/triangulation and all lighting environments are not certified. No unsupported fullbright adjustment was assumed.",
      "Replacement and final release frames are close to the actual stone anchor after pulling, so they establish a limited camera view. They do not independently display the removed old hook, the entire replacement trajectory or every release angle; native logs establish the ownership transition and two releases.",
      "All11 original PNG and both sheets were reviewed, but this does not cover every model angle, random glow frame, FOV setting, texture pack, all charge-HUD states or every target/portal/entity collision."
    ]
